# Step 3.3 — create a team (Flow 6). Run `bun run dev`; VS Code "REST Client" keeps cookies.
# Needs a registered participant with no team (participants.http). Every create needs an
# `Idempotency-Key` header: a new UUID per action ({{$guid}}); resending the same key replays.
@base = http://localhost:3000
@origin = http://localhost:3000
@hackathon = hackfest-2026
# Change this before re-running the replay demo (keys are kept 24 h).
@key = demo-create-team-0001

### Sign in
POST {{base}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "email": "pat@example.com", "password": "REPLACE_ME" }

### Create → 201 with the team + its invite code (shown to the creator only)
POST {{base}}/api/hackathons/{{hackathon}}/teams
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
Idempotency-Key: {{key}}

{
  "name": "Rocket   Team",
  "description": "Building a race-proof team finder.",
  "joinPolicy": "APPROVAL",
  "access": "PUBLIC",
  "inviteExpiresInHours": 72
}

### Same key again → the SAME 201 (same invite code) + `Idempotent-Replayed: true`
POST {{base}}/api/hackathons/{{hackathon}}/teams
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
Idempotency-Key: {{key}}

{
  "name": "Rocket   Team",
  "description": "Building a race-proof team finder.",
  "joinPolicy": "APPROVAL",
  "access": "PUBLIC",
  "inviteExpiresInHours": 72
}

### New key → a new action → 409 ALREADY_IN_TEAM
POST {{base}}/api/hackathons/{{hackathon}}/teams
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{ "name": "Second Team", "joinPolicy": "OPEN", "access": "PUBLIC" }

### My status → team: { id, name, isLeader: true }
GET {{base}}/api/hackathons/{{hackathon}}/me

### Invalid → 400 (name too short, unknown policy, hours out of range, unknown field)
POST {{base}}/api/hackathons/{{hackathon}}/teams
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{ "name": "ab", "joinPolicy": "SOMETIMES", "access": "PUBLIC", "inviteExpiresInHours": 721, "color": "red" }

### Another user, same name in other letter case → 409 TEAM_NAME_TAKEN
# (sign in as that user first; they must be registered and not in a team)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Step 3.4 — join (Flow 1)
# Sign in as someone registered in the hackathon and not in a team there.
@teamId = REPLACE_WITH_AN_OPEN_PUBLIC_TEAM_ID

### Join from the board (OPEN + PUBLIC teams only) → 200 { team, joinedAt }
POST {{base}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/join
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{}

### Join with an invite code (any access). Case, hyphens, spaces and I/L/O look-alikes are
### forgiven. Any bad code (wrong, malformed, revoked, expired) → the same 404 INVALID_CODE.
### An APPROVAL team's code → 409 APPROVAL_REQUIRED (until step 4.2 adds join requests).
POST {{base}}/api/invites/redeem
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{ "code": "abcde-12345" }

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Step 3.5 — leave (Flow 3)
# 200 { teamId, teamDeleted, newLeader }. Last member → team deleted (R7). Leader leaving →
# the longest-joined member leads (R6), returned in `newLeader`. Not in this team → 409
# NOT_A_MEMBER; not registered in its hackathon → 403 NOT_REGISTERED.
POST {{base}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/leave
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Step 3.6 — reads (05 §3–4)
# Lists: newest first; params cursor, limit (1-50, default 20), policy, access, q (name search).
# Response { data: { teams: [cards], totalCount }, nextCursor }. Pass nextCursor back unchanged.

### Board: listed teams only (looking AND not full)
GET {{base}}/api/hackathons/{{hackathon}}/board?limit=10

### All Teams, filtered + searched (q is matched literally: % and _ are not wildcards)
GET {{base}}/api/hackathons/{{hackathon}}/teams?policy=OPEN&access=PUBLIC&q=rocket

### Next page: copy nextCursor from the previous response
GET {{base}}/api/hackathons/{{hackathon}}/teams?limit=10&cursor=PASTE_NEXT_CURSOR

### Team page: card + members (join order) + viewer { isMember, isLeader, myRequest }
GET {{base}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}

### Hackathon detail: stats { participants, teams, lookingTeams } (lookingTeams = board total)
GET {{base}}/api/hackathons/{{hackathon}}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Step 4.2 — join requests (Flow 4)
# APPROVAL + PUBLIC teams from the board; INVITE_ONLY ones via their code (redeem, above):
# redeem answers 200 { outcome: "JOINED", … } for OPEN teams, 201 { outcome: "REQUESTED", request }
# for APPROVAL teams. OPEN team here → 409 USE_JOIN; again → 409 REQUEST_ALREADY_PENDING;
# after a leader decline → 409 PREVIOUSLY_DECLINED (R13); full team → 409 TEAM_FULL.

### Request to join → 201 { request: { id, teamId, hackathonId, status: "PENDING", createdAt } }
POST {{base}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/requests
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{}
